+2. **Derive Axis-Aligned Affine:** Using the public affine API, replace `volume.hdr.affine` with its nearest axis-aligned equivalent derived from `volume.originalAffine` [S1, unofficial]. Preserve each voxel axis's dominant direction, sign, and length to prevent data permutation or mirroring [S1, unofficial]. Ensure the world origin remains on the same voxel to prevent crosshair jumps during toggling [S1, unofficial]. The core system then derives an identity `obliqueRAS` from the new affine, laying slices back on the voxel grid [S1, unofficial].
 3. **Apply to Canvas:** The correction is derived from the background volume's `originalAffine` and applied to all volumes on the canvas to maintain registration [S1, unofficial].
 4. **Handle Overlays:** If overlays are added while in voxel-space mode, re-emit `nvArray` via the overlay message handler to ensure they use the corrected affine and stay registered [S1, unofficial].
 5. **Reset:** To restore world-space rendering, call `resetVolumeAffine` to restore the original `hdr.affine` exactly [S1, unofficial].
 
+**Formulas:**
+The axis-aligned affine $A_{aligned}$ is derived from the original affine $A$ by zeroing off-diagonal elements while preserving the diagonal scales/signs and the translation row:
+$$A_{aligned}[i][j] = \begin{cases} A[i][j] & \text{if } i = j \text{ or } i = 3 \\ 0 & \text{otherwise} \end{cases}$$
+where $i,j \in \{0,1,2,3\}$ and the matrix layout follows the library's row-major convention [S1, unofficial].
+
